    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d316">

                <pb facs="0538" n="436" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg436"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.114 Norway/16a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Norway</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Biddle</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-11-12T16:00:00-05:00">November 12,
                            1935—4 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>16. No reply received to instruction No. 300, July 5, 1935. Telegraph action
                    taken. Endeavor expedite reply and inform Norwegian Government also that
                    Norwegian steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Trajan</hi> unloaded nearly 15,000
                    cases alcohol on high seas into four or five smuggling vessels in August, and
                    that Norwegian steamer <hi rendition="#italic">Reidun</hi> is at present
                    unloading nearly 20,000 cases alcohol on high seas into smuggling vessels.
                    Several United States Coast Guard vessels are standing by, observing
                    procedure.</p>
                <pb facs="0539" n="437" xml:id="pg437"/>
                <p>Suggest action of Norwegian vessels appears to be contrary to Norwegian law
                    regarding participation in smuggling directed against foreign country.</p>
                <p>Details of unloading contained in instruction No. 13, November 4, 1935.<anchor
                        n="71" xml:id="d316-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
